      },
      "message": "feat(ui): add Shift snapping and typed values to viewport bar\n\nComplete slice (d) of #1198 after the control bar (PR #1203), move\nhandles (PR #1330), and rotate rings (#2047, PR #2185).\n\nExpand the bottom overlay bar upward only when Move or Rotate mode is\nactive. Show an axis selector (X, Y, Z), a typed distance or angle box\nwith Set / Enter commit, and an editable Shift-snap step parameter\n(1.0 mm default for Move through the unit lens, 90.0 deg default for\nRotate). Live drags update the bar value and track unsnapped raw\ndelta/angle so Shift toggles smoothly; typed values queue the same\nMoveModelBy / TurnModelBy commands (one MoveModel undo step).\n\nDecision record: docs/decisions/1198-bar-snap-and-value.md.\n\nFixes #1198\n\nCo-Authored-By: Antigravity <noreply@google.com>",
